Parliament will hold the final vote on  two Landmark bills the Digital Services  Act and the digital markets act they'll  provide a fairer online framework  limiting the powers of big internet  platforms like search engines and make  digital markets safer and more  competitive  MEPS will discuss the recent decision to  Grant Ukraine and Moldova EU candidate  status a move backed by parliament in  June they'll also assess developments in  three accession countries in the western  Balkans  members will decide whether to veto  commission plans to list certain nuclear  and gas projects as environmentally  sustainable if voted down the commission  would need to redraft or withdraw the  so-called taxonomy rules  Czech prime minister Petra fiala will  outline his country's priorities for the  next six months as Prague takes over the  rotating presidency of the council from  France  Parliament will vote on its proposals to  better support mental health in the age  of digital technology and homeworking  MEPS argue that while both bring  benefits more should be done to improve  work-life balance and prevent stress  anxiety and depression  [Music]
 

